      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(skills): reject skill downloads exceeding 100 MB",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`downloadFile()` streams response body to disk via pipeline without a\nbyte limit. A hostile server can send unbounded data, filling the disk.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdded `SKILL_DOWNLOAD_MAX_BYTES` (100 MB) and a post-download file size\ncheck. If the temp file exceeds the limit, it is rejected with a clear\nerror before the file is consumed by downstream extraction.\n\n## User Impact\n\n**Before:** No size limit — unbounded disk usage\n**After:** Downloads over 100 MB rejected with error message\n\n## Evidence\n\nBranch: `fix/install-download-maxbytes` | Base: `upstream/main` | Node: v22.19.0 Linux x64\n\n### Regression tests\n\n```\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/skills/lifecycle/install-download.test.ts\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  7 passed (7)\n```\n\n### Live proof: node --import tsx\n\nImport OK — production module loads, SKILL_DOWNLOAD_MAX_BYTES = 100 MB\n\n### Checks\n\n- oxfmt — passed\n- oxlint — passed\n- git diff --check — passed\n\n### Diff\n\n```\nsrc/skills/lifecycle/install-download.ts | 9 +++++ (constant + post-download size check)\n```\n\n- [x] I understand what the code does\n- [x] Change is focused and does not mix unrelated concerns",
        "branch": "fix/install-download-maxbytes",
